        <Document ID="3B14DCBD-3454-4C9F-A9A9-C9AEB222DD36">
            <Title>Sherpa Rifle</Title>
            <Text>Sherpa Rifle

Round capacity: Magazine-fed; exact capacity not stated.
Role in Story: Standard Protectant rifle for John's team, especially during cold-weather and mountain deployments.
Proficient Characters: John Walker, Tex Kovachnikov, Tao Vang, Shai Siante.
Season: Chapters 1-4.
Unique Features: Sherpa cold-weather configuration, integrated thermal core, reversible cooling cycle, and strong resistance to condensation or cold-weather jamming.
Description: The Sherpa configuration is a Protectant rifle tuned for extreme environments. In the Himalayas John uses reverse thermal mode to melt through ice and reveal the buried facility, and the platform remains the squad's dependable long gun even after the Mark IV introduces more autonomous fire support.
Sights: Amber and red HUD icons, blue flame when reverse thermal mode is engaged, and a clean lattice stock.
Sounds: Mechanical click, cooling-cycle hiss and the crack of a live weapon in thin air.
Smell: Steam, hot metal and burnt frost.
Notes: The manuscript also treats the rifle as an extension of John's field habits: familiar, maintained and trusted.
Built at: Protectant arsenal.
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="3F1E5B90-D488-4545-8104-17E78D691A45">
            <Title>Tao Vang</Title>
            <Text>Tao Vang

Ethnicity: Not clearly stated in manuscript.
Position: Lieutenant, engineer and team tech.
Age: 32.
Sex: Female.
Height: Not stated.
Build: Not stated.
Role in Story: John's technical backbone. Tao keeps the squad's suits, weapons, sensors and ships operational and is usually the first person solving a systems failure under pressure.
Goal: Keep the team alive through engineering discipline and make sense of every black-box system put in front of her.
Physical Description: Carries herself with clean precision and confident posture. Her expression hardens quickly when she does not trust a system.
Personality: Analytical, skeptical, disciplined and dryly funny. She is confident in her engineering judgment and protective of the people who depend on it.
Occupation: Protectant engineer and field systems specialist.
Habits/Mannerisms: Takes notes constantly. Answers technical questions directly. Pushes back on unsafe assumptions even when John is briefing the room.
Background: Based on Ceres and integrated into John's squad as its resident engineer. She handles hacking, suit logic, sensor interpretation and rail-weapon systems.
Internal Conflicts: She wants to trust progress, but she mistrusts any technology whose limits have not been honestly explained.
External Conflicts: Marcellus's secrecy repeatedly forces her to work blind, from the lost facility to the Europa operations.
Notes: The manuscript alternates between &quot;Tao&quot; and &quot;Tau&quot;; both clearly refer to the same character.
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="3F337436-E66E-48DF-A2BC-C3B7FD4AD50A">
            <Title>Cover</Title>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="42279CFD-46D4-444A-9D6C-D9D1F3CB5869">
