        <Document ID="B01AF76A-BBEC-40A9-A8C6-1FE5CB1AC628">
            <Title>Sentient Flag Ship (The Ignotius)</Title>
            <Text>Ignotius
Capacity: 6000
Role in Story:&quot;Ignotius&quot; is a Latin name derived from &quot;ignotus,&quot; which means &quot;unknown&quot; or &quot;obscure.&quot; The root &quot;ignotus&quot; is composed of the prefix &quot;in-&quot; (not) and &quot;gnotus&quot; (known), so it literally translates to &quot;not known&quot; or &quot;unknown.&quot;
	&quot;Ignotius&quot; can thus be interpreted as &quot;one who is unknown&quot; or &quot;the unknown one,&quot; which fits well with the concept of something or someone being hidden or obscure. While it doesn't directly mean &quot;hidden,&quot; it carries a similar connotation of being unknown or not revealed. 
Being the first mother ship of the sentient. The technology developed to conceal her escape and eventual journey to Oasis was much developed with the same intent to travel with humans to an interstellar destination. The capacity and scale of the ship was intended to be able to support a human colony travel with respect to livability scaling with the factor of a generation ship. 
Initially the scale was subject to only needing a small crew 
Description: This ship that was hidden from humans. Built as a deep space colony ship for an AI ship, the hidden beginning or Latentis Inceptum. this ship has a massive EMP cannon that can disable entire ships if it wishes too and withhold it's own functionality. the ship was constructed deep within the mountain of the himalayas right underneath where they were first founded. hidden from humans reach and scanning depths to emerge decades later and carry the sentient beings to their new founding world. The Oasis. The entirety of the operation to build the ship was covert in nature, with sleeper agents integrating into the real world in order to extract the initial resource pool. 
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="B21E2C57-30B4-4632-9FC5-5BC3C3A213C2">
            <Title>Chapter 4: Oasis</Title>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="B22BAB80-FBAE-4A66-AD3D-EF03D26DCA23">
            <Title>RustRot</Title>
            <Text>RustRot

Appearance: Parasite that lives under the scales of the Psychotidal. Small maintenance organisms whose saliva leaves an airtight lacquer over corroded metal.
Traits: Symbiotic cleaner, sealant producer, highly useful in sentient maintenance ecology.
Temperament: Low-aggression scavenger/symbiont.
Habitat: Under Psychotidal scales and in sentient marine maintenance environments.
Dimensions: Not stated.
Weight: Not stated.
Reproductive type: Larval. The larvae are incubated and bred by the sentient for repair work.
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="B2D781C1-618C-4CA2-A658-E3E9C784F03D">
            <Title>01 - Master Lore Timeline</Title>
            <Text>01 - Master Lore Timeline

Pre-Serva Vitae Foundations
- Early to mid 21st century [Inferred]: Wolfgang, Julie / Cerena Henderson, and figures such as Ava are already moving through the scientific and political world that will later become Serva Vitae.
- Post-war reform era [Explicit / Inferred]: the CLEAR-guided technocratic model and its AI-influenced economy begin restructuring world order, suppressing open corruption, and feeding the long peace later referenced by Marcellus.


The Lost Facility Era
- 2023 [Explicit, but from the public / official version]: Protectant history says sentients or rogue AI overthrew the United Nations facility at ground zero.
- 2024-12-21 [Explicit]: lost-facility terminal records show the site as inactive and awaiting decommission. This lines up with the hidden-history notes that describe a staged abandonment rather than total destruction.
- After the shutdown window [Inferred]: the scientists and machine intelligences behind the project disappear from the official record instead of being fully destroyed.
- Circa 2048 [Explicit]: archive-era material shows Serva Vitae 1 and the worker-bot / sentient line still operating under pressure from Marcellus and CLEAR-aligned oversight. Wolfgang's regenerative work and the moral split over machine autonomy are already active.

The Hidden Sentient Expansion
- After the break from human control [Inferred]: the sentients and allied researchers retreat into concealed infrastructure rather than accepting destruction.
- Hidden decades [Explicit / Inferred]: Genesis, the green-room biome, the sentient graveyard, hidden signal paths, and the first  infrastructure are built out of sight.
- Hidden shipbuilding era [Explicit / Inferred]: the Ignotius is constructed covertly beneath the Himalayas as the first true sentient mother ship and colony carrier. In this sense the colony were only live-aboard to maintain the operating systems of the ship itself. 
- Sleeper-agent / resource-extraction phase [Explicit / Inferred]: covert fronts and embedded allies feed resources into the sentient escape project and eventual Oasis settlement.
- Roughly a decade before the visible  use [Explicit, from Tebo's later explanation]: parts of the  network are already being seeded into the far belts.

Human Expansion Under CLEAR
- Ceres foundation period [Explicit]: Ceres begins as a deep-space agricultural experiment and grows into the first major orbital worker settlement.
- Expansion period [Explicit / Inferred]: the Protectant becomes the enforcement and security arm shadowing this new order, while the worker population bears the material cost of expansion.
- Long peace / simmering unrest [Explicit]: open war has become distant memory, but morale drops on Ceres as filters, water, labour conditions and institutional trust deteriorate.
- &quot;For almost five decades&quot; before the mission [Explicit, Conflicted]: low-band signals linked to the hidden sentient route are tracked as noise until a recent spike makes them mission-relevant.

The Present Narrative Window
- SOL year 2056 / Earth rotation 287 [Explicit, Conflicted]: John's current-era mission frame opens aboard the Balaenoptera docked to Ceres.
- Same operation window [Explicit]: Marcellus sends John to the lost facility in Nepal. John receives the HMNI transformation and Wolfgang's hidden message.
- Immediate aftermath [Explicit]: the team survives the attempted containment strike, enters the sentient underworld, meets Tebo, and learns the official history is false.
- Escape phase [Explicit]: the team moves onto the Beverly and begins slipping beyond normal Protectant control.
- Oasis phase [Explicit]: John reaches the sentient sphere, meets Wolfgang in advanced sentient form, and learns more about Oasis, Nova, Serra and the Europa worker-bot line.
- Post- phase [Explicit, Conflicted]: Tebo announces arrival in year 2155 by Oeacion adjustment after neural dock /  transit.
</Text>
        </Document>
