        <Document ID="CCFF3286-A203-4EB4-85AF-870FF79F7D8E">
            <Title>Overhauled Sentient/Protectant Science research vessel (The Beverly)</Title>
            <Text>The Beverly

Capacity: 12.
Role in Story: Hybrid science and escape vessel that carries John's team out of Protectant reach and deeper into the sentient arc.
Related Characters: John Walker, Nova Serra, G Wolfgang, Tebo, Tao Vang, Shai Siante, Tex Kovachnikov.
Season: Chapters 3-4.
Unique Features: Sentient/Protectant hybrid systems, storm rail cannon, PDC coverage, cloak-capable escape profile, gate-compatible hardware, and self-healing nanometallic hull memory.
Description: The Beverly is an overhauled research vessel tied to John's family history and the Serva Vitae project. Small, nostalgic and far more advanced than it first appears, it carries hidden sentient engineering inside a compact shell. Later upgrades give the hull regenerative memory and allow damage to seal over in seconds.
Sights: Smooth stealth-bird contours, a cramped cockpit, living-looking inner hull and repaired battle scars disappearing back into the plating.
Sounds: Charging coils, vacuum systems, bridge hum and the hard clap of the mounted storm rail.
Smell: Sterile metal, warm electronics and the faint ozone of heavily worked systems.
Notes: Named after John's childhood horse. The ship symbolizes the continuity between his mother's work, the sentient escape and John's own passage into the next phase of the story.
Built at: Serva Vitae / lost-facility research lineage.
</Text>
        </Document>
