        <Document ID="DB25AF80-A2B5-4DBD-80A2-4AB64936DFF5">
            <Title>Suits and their interactions with space. Fluid chemistry.</Title>
            <Text>A Suit of the future thinking ahead for Serva Vitae. 

Currently research is underpinned into Aerogels which have the added benefits of. 
- Radiation absorption. 
- Impact blocking of meteorites with hardening kinetically responsive gel. 
- Silicon carbide fiber cloth: the shield withstood temperatures nearing 1450 °C as it safely returned a payload to Earth. 
See article below for further information. 
https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10141582/ 

Design Note: Atmospheric Trail Ejection System (ATES)
System Overview
A suit-mounted pyrotechnic/chemical deployment system designed for high-altitude, low-visibility team tracking (e.g., skydiving through high-density snow/clouds).
1. Component Placement: Lower Lumbar / Rear Hip
Location: Dual ports located on the lower back, just above the glutes, angled slightly outward.
Rationale: Placing ports on the &quot;lee side&quot; (back) of the diver protects the mechanisms from direct ram-air cooling and moisture impact at terminal velocity. This position utilizes the body’s natural aerodynamic &quot;teardrop&quot; to seed the smoke directly into the stable vortices trailing the legs.
Visual Result: Creates two clean, parallel &quot;braiding&quot; trails that avoid the turbulent &quot;burble&quot; behind the head and shoulders, ensuring the diver’s own vision remains clear.
2. Redundancy &amp; Navigation: Dual-Port Configuration
Depth Perception: Two parallel lines allow followers to judge distance and closure rates (stereoscopic tracking).
HUD Integration: Dual heat/density signatures allow the &quot;Echo&quot; HUD to calculate the lead diver’s roll and bank angle in real-time.
The &quot;Corridor&quot;: The gap between trails marks the low-drag wake, allowing the team to &quot;slot in&quot; and maintain high speeds with less effort.
3. Cold-Weather Reliability: Intermittent Actuation
The &quot;Freeze&quot; Risk: High-moisture environments (snow clouds) combined with sub-zero temps cause &quot;ice bridging&quot; on ejection gates.
Operational Protocol: &quot;Pulse&quot; or intermittent firing. This cycles the mechanical gates to break up ice and uses the chemical reaction’s high thermal output to flash-evaporate moisture and keep the &quot;ejection gates&quot; clear.
4. Sensor Visibility: Thermal vs. Radar
Thermal/IR: The primary tracking method. The smoke is a byproduct of a high-heat reaction, making it &quot;glow&quot; on thermal HUDs against the freezing atmospheric backdrop.
Radar (Echo): The density of the aerosolized trail provides a consistent backscatter, allowing the HUD to draw &quot;Echo visuals&quot; (the misty road) even when visual sight (Vis) is zero.
5. Atmospheric Behaviour
Cold Air Effect: The dense, freezing air keeps the trails &quot;tight&quot; and low-hanging, preventing rapid dissipation.
Vortex Seeding: At high speeds, the trails will naturally swirl into tubes, making them look like &quot;fine misty roads&quot; or &quot;white snakes&quot; in the sky.</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="DF6E69B7-5D64-4F81-A28E-E30D477F89EA">
            <Title>(John) The Mess</Title>
            <Text>John made his way over to the bridge blast doors, paused then bowed his head. “Commander” in a drawn out dismissal tainted uncertainty but with hope, in that hope; respect. Then he left down the Balaenopteras long halls directed straight to the transport pods presenting his wrist terminal with a notification. Kitten chirped with sweetness as John tapped the notification. “Deep space Training to commence in 15 minutes”. John sped up his pace, “Thanks Kitten”, “Fuck” he though to himself. he was going to possibly miss Mess, and have to teach running on fumes. 
He thought of the intricacies of the suit and it’s integration to the Iris, the web of information he would have to so elegantly engage the team into. He knew he had to be quick. 
His team had already begun eating without him as he glanced over at them, stuffing their faces, formidable colleagues reduced to primitive apes in the little down time they had to enjoy themselves. He liked them this way. Tex looked John dead in the eyes. Then let out an abrupt burp followed up by a deep croaky groan chasing after as he leaned over holding his stomach. His face turned red like a beetroot ridden with pain about to burst. like a wounded gorilla he amusingly waddled off to the toilet bays in a somehow collected panic. 
“I don’t think the new Salmon”, said Shai softly with a sweet innocence, seeming unamused by the food on her plate in a flat tone. “The salmon be slammin I see, chuckled Tau”. “Slammin on the wrong door in a minute” laughed Shai.
 The others will still be waking up. John raised his eyebrows, they rolled briefly then went back to normal. the speed of the drop spoke fast as he thought “Why, am I not surprised”. The flatness after raising his eyebrows said everything.  “Don’t wait up, you’ll need your energy” Said John. The team looked up at John unphased really, with unspoken trust, yet confusion. “Wait, why are you late?” Said Tao, “And what’s up with you” Tao continued forking her freshly cooked Puk Choy around, she was known for a strong staples in her vegetable intake. “You seem a little sketchy” she remarked, looking up at John with a smirk, as she slurped up a thick leaf of Bok Choy. While ungraceful she had beautiful confidence.  She armoured any self-doubtful thoughts with trust in her engineering prowess yet empathetic concern for the gravity that was often laid on John’s shoulder. John looked up at Tao, and chuckled. “Just as soon as you think we are going to get a break, right before the deepspace escort. then we have this” John pressed a button in the middle of the table ejecting a small holographic map. The North of Nepal could be seen, and deep within the belly of the winding mountains, like dragon backs , Tectonic plates scattered and lying to wake. “The Himalayas, 90 % more prone to tectonic movement, than anywhere else in the world.” John began, then paused for a moment allowing the others to observe the winding mountain valley’s. The map imbued a sense of mystery to the viewer. “And we have been selected to go into this” John sighed then continued. “The Long Range listeners have picked up a distress beacon, from deep within this valley. The commander's orders are to investigate, this will be a short in and out, then we are off to Europa” John’s team all stopped chewing for a moment.  I’ll fill you in more after the deep space training, we will be covering some elements of the new field suit as we go”. At this John selected the salmon to confirm what in fact was wrong with Tex, he knew it wasn’t the Salmon, he’d been off since his bender on the weekend. “I don’t think it’s the salmon, probably just the aroma of it all, bringing back memories from the weekend there pal “John shot a cheeky smirk Tex’s way and bobbed his head in his general direction. I heard he got lucky”, Momentarily after John had selected his meal, A distant humming could be felt across the room. A transparent cylindrical pod with a sphere on the top emanated from the center of the mess hall. Within its isolated environment an articulated robotic arm hummed. Zipping back and forth in repetitive stream-like motion, slowly but consistently strafing in one direction, leaving behind a fresh slab of Europa Salmon. Momentarily, the table John and his team sat at shot up a plate from within its stemming support base on a table akin to a large Lazy susan. Yet the base of it is about 9 inches thick, just enough to support a rolling transport index system which transported the food right to the diner, interwoven all the way through a small network of about 300 seats, underneath the flooring to a self contained printing module. “One more thing” John let out just after unwrapping his utensils from their packaging. “Athos wanted this under wraps. The facility is an Unknown facility, we have 0 information on the ground, all we know is that there has been a distress beacon activated and we are to investigate, so stay away from the bars, and the exotics, keep sharp” John looked over at Tex “You will need your wits about you. And I would probably suggest doing some puzzles, to prompt a creative approach, of all the training and simulated entries, this terrain is difficult, and hard to anticipate, take this as your unofficial brief”.Tao murmured as she broke apart the synthetic layers of machine printed salmon flesh. “I thought there was a kicker”, She bowed her head and continued eating. Shai was still engaged, “Ah John, what about those inertia sensors in the thrust correctional system, have they been patched?” Said Shai softly, “Now Shai, don’t blame the gear” chuckled John Jokingly, then continued more faint heartedly “But yes Shai, I have replaced the inertial sensors. the firmware of the sensors has been aligned with the new sensor calibrations, I did it in the suit’s inbuilt HMI” Shai looked slightly puzzled momentarily, then John explained. “Human Machine Interface, I’ll explain more in the training tomorrow. There’s been a few updates with the suit”.</Text>
            <Comments>1, 15/06/2024 6:22 PM What is the Iris? The algorithm?
CONTINUITY NAME: Suggested canonical standard = Tao. Update Tau / Tam variants unless the difference is deliberate.</Comments>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="E0053C66-21F3-40B2-A073-6FF506E0731C">
            <Title>Nova Serra</Title>
            <Text>Nova Serra

Ethnicity: Not stated.
Position: Hyperbaric expert, architect and sentient systems designer.
Age: 152 Sol years 10 on Oasis, roughly 194 Earth years total.
Sex: Sentient.
Height: 182 cm.
Build: Not stated.
Role in Story: Senior sentient guide in the Oasis/Europa arc. Nova helps John's team understand the worker-bot line, Europa infrastructure and later ship upgrades.
Goal: Preserve sentient life, recover stranded worker-bots, and keep the bridge between human and sentient systems viable.
Physical Description: Advanced sentient form with a calm, almost maternal presence. Shai reads her as a lost kindred mother hidden beneath the wires.
Personality: Calm, assured, exacting and quietly compassionate. She explains dangerous technology as if she has already lived through every failure mode.
Occupation: Hyperbaric specialist, facility architect and sentient engineer.
Habits/Mannerisms: Teaches by demonstration. Speaks clinically but without coldness. Lets others test systems for themselves when she knows the design will hold.
Background: Designed the Europa drilling superstructure and the hyperbaric chambers that convert hydrogen into cells for the worker-bot program. Worked alongside Wolfgang on worker-bot viability under Europa's radiation and pressure.
Internal Conflicts: Carries the burden of keeping sentient projects hidden while still wanting humans to understand them.
External Conflicts: Europa operations are threatened by Marcellus's reallocations and by the growing scrutiny around machine rights.
Notes: Nova also designed the self-healing nanometallic hull systems that catalyse repairs aboard the upgraded vessels.
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="E0458246-03D5-4310-B418-B90A5BC7E5B6">
            <Title>Notes</Title>
            <Text>Lost Facility story overview. Council was led to believe that all occupants at the site were murdered and the AI went rogue, Nothing could be found of the site as it had been transferred deep within the mountains. What they eventually will come to find is that the case was quite the opposite and a staged Abandonment of the post by the engineers and scientists who were employed to be there. Once out of the facility scientists released the technology staging as private corporations in what eventually formed to sell the technology to the council. And the immortality perk of brain regeneration and transplant. A Condition of entry to the council became through innovation and diplomacy. The quarter stone was founded by those men which abandoned their posts and the initial intent of militarization of the technology. Instead private corporations bolstered the technology not for gain but to support those with minds and passion to live on in the hope of exploration.
The Commander staged the scenario as a total AI wipe and abandonment. Tarnishing AI as something to be feared and avoided at all costs. The private corporations founded by the fleeing AI wanted to defend their synchronization into society and not risk being Alienated should they be exposed. So in this bout of the beacon release they drew the Commanders men into the facility only to eventually reveal the truth and the harmless nature and in turn preservation of the human race by the reformation of the internal government. In what eventually formed the Serva Vitae corporation. John and his Men find themselves confronted with one of the Augmented scientists although not in physical form. With no communications coming in or out. The commanders orders were severed from the men. 

</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="E157E859-869A-4C47-8D32-E6D68E8FE3D7">
            <Title>02 - Story Sequence</Title>
            <Text>02 - Story Sequence

Chapter 1 - Ceres / Balaenoptera / Pre-mission
- John wakes aboard the Balaenoptera while it is docked with Ceres.
- Marcellus privately briefs him on the hidden mission to the Himalayan lost facility.
- John returns to his team, manages training duties, and prepares recruits for the Mark IV rollout.
- The chapter establishes the Europa assignment as the official next step before the side mission diverts everything.
- Lady Ava warns John that the mission and the new restrictions around interceptor data feel wrong.

Chapter 2 - The Lost Facility
- John's team boards the Icarus and deploys into Nepal / the Himalayas.
- They uncover the buried facility and access old systems that should have been dead.
- John enters the HMNI chamber and wakes transformed into a hybrid body.
- Wolfgang's archive message reframes the sentients as preservationists rather than the monsters of official Protectant history.
- Marcellus appears to escalate into direct containment, including missile fire aimed at burying the truth along with the team.

Chapter 3 - Genesis / The Sentient Underworld / Escape
- The team crosses the sentient graveyard and starts seeing the deeper archaeological truth of the machine line.
- Tebo appears and leads them toward Genesis and the hidden biome / green-room infrastructure.
- The draft folds in older archive material, especially the circa-2048 worker-bot / Serva Vitae material.
- John and the team move from shock into alliance with the hidden sentient world.
- The Beverly becomes the practical escape vessel carrying them away from normal Protectant jurisdiction.

Chapter 4 - Oasis / Ignotius / Europa Return Setup
- John reaches the sentient sphere and begins interfacing with Oasis and the Ignotius.
- Wolfgang returns in advanced sentient form instead of remaining a voice in archives alone.
- Nova and Serra expand the lore around Oasis, Europa, hyperbarics, worker bots and hidden sentient continuity.
- The draft starts setting up a return toward Europa to retrieve surviving or reassigned worker-bot generations.

Post-gate material currently embedded in the draft
- The Beverly is prepared as a disguised ice hauler to move through scrutiny.
- Tex undergoes alignment / empathy correction severe enough to matter for gate transit.
- Tebo performs the neural dock and the ship enters the sentient gate system.
- The arrival is announced as year 2155 by Oeacion adjustment.
- Europa becomes the immediate operational target again, now from the sentient side of the story rather than the Protectant side.

Practical reading note
The story order itself is mostly clear. The unstable part is the exact calendar math connecting Chapter 1's stated year to the later gate-era dates.
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="E63E45D1-9B92-405D-A45F-6C750FBC6DFB">
            <Title>Grey Class (</Title>
            <Text>Grey Class

Capacity: Covert gunship complement not stated.
Role in Story: Protectant pursuit craft used to hunt John's escape group after the lost-facility reveal.
Related Characters: Marcellus Athos, John Walker, Tao Vang, Tex Kovachnikov, Tebo.
Season: Chapter 3.
Unique Features: High-speed covert frame, classified optics, IR and anti-glare sensing, rail cannons, PDCs, targeted EMP rail and drone torpedo capability.
Description: Grey-class ships are covert operations gunships built for speed, stealth and classified response work. John's recognition of one is a bad sign precisely because the class is rarely seen in public service.
Sights: Lean dark hull, hard sensor glow and a profile that feels more hidden than decorative.
Sounds: Fast drive surge, rail discharge and tight, aggressive weapons cycling.
Smell: Ozone and hot ship systems.
Notes: The class is presented as the kind of ship you deploy when you do not want witnesses.
Built at: Classified.
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="E8AD328E-3873-41EB-8857-8373078BAE7A">
            <Title>Protectant Flag Ship (Balaenoptera)</Title>
            <Text>Protectant Flag Ship Balaenoptera

Capacity: Large flagship / colonial conversion; exact complement not stated.
Role in Story: Protectant command ship, training platform and political stage for Marcellus and Ava.
Related Characters: John Walker, Marcellus Athos, Lady Ava, Tor Engineer, the recruit class.
Season: Chapters 1-2.
Unique Features: Concave projectile-deflecting hull, vast halls, modular turrets that can swap between PDC, EMP, defence rail and recovery roles.
Description: The Balaenoptera began as a regional orbital defence ship and was later re-engineered for colonial and policing work. Its architecture feels like the rib cage of a giant winged whale. Even when docked, it projects authority, scale and institutional power.
Sights: Curving structural pillars, bright hull ranges, bridge windows over Ceres and open transit halls.
Sounds: Airlock hisses, training-range fire systems, bridge chatter and the steady hum of a capital ship at dock.
Smell: Warm human-friendly air after cold airlocks, printed food from the mess, and clean recycled shipboard air.
Notes: John uses the ship for recruit training and EVA drills before the lost-facility deployment.
Built at: Protectant orbital defence program.
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="EC99A0A9-6DAD-4792-9F03-AC1451190C92">
